ai-self-study license scope

Original educational text in book/chapters, book/sections, book/references.tex,
README.md, docs/, research/, papers/studies/, original figures and numerical
results, and original QA findings: Creative Commons Attribution 4.0
International (CC BY 4.0), see licenses/CC-BY-4.0.txt.
Attribution: ai-self-study contributors, repository ai-self-study.

Original Python, Shell, and test code in experiments/, scripts/, and tests/:
MIT License, see licenses/MIT.txt.

Selected unofficial paper translations and attributed paper figures in
papers/translations/ are adaptations under the exact source versions' CC BY
4.0 licenses. See papers/rights.json and each paper's metadata and figure
credits. Preserve original authors, source, license and modification notices.
DGM manuscript code excerpts and patches under papers/translations/dgm/code/
are covered by the source manuscript's license, not this project's MIT grant.
Do not execute manuscript examples as part of building or testing this project.

The fixed adapter embedded in book/main.tex was supplied through the user's
explicitly requested math-latex-typesetting skill and is distributed with this
authorized source delivery. It is not the official ElegantBook class. Its
original provider's rights are retained; the project's MIT or CC BY grant does
not independently relicense that inherited template. See docs/third-party.md.

External papers and books not selected for licensed translation, fonts,
software dependencies, downloaded model weights and datasets retain their
own licenses. No English source paper/book PDF, model weights, copied course
assignment or installable font is bundled. Linking does not relicense a source.
